<title>AUSTRALIA: SFE wheat steady as weather fails to lead.</title>
<headline>SFE wheat steady as weather fails to lead.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sydney Futures Exchange (SFE) wheat futures held steady on Tuesday after patchy weekend rain failed to improve drought-affected 1997/98 crop prospects.</p>
<p>January 1998 sold 19 lots at a steady A$193.50 a tonne.  Two put options also sold on January 1998 at an exercise price of A$170.00 for a A$3.00 premium.</p>
<p>Settlement prices in untraded contracts were mostly steady.</p>
<p>Chris Gray of C,A &amp; L Bell Commodities Corp said not enough rain fell over the weekend to drive wheat futures prices down.</p>
<p>Steady prices were expected for the next few days, with some growers considering exiting long positions, he said.  </p>
